From: Carlos López <clopez@suse.de>
Patch-mainline: never, kabi
References: jsc#PED-16823
Subject: [PATCH] kABI fix for KVM: arm64: Introduce
 KVM_REG_ARM_VENDOR_HYP_BMAP_2

Commit c0000e58c74e ("KVM: arm64: Introduce KVM_REG_ARM_VENDOR_HYP_BMAP_2")
adds the vendor_hyp_bmap_2 field to struct kvm_smccc_features, which is
embedded in struct kvm_arch, which in turn is embedded in struct kvm.
This changes the symbol versions of kvm_get_kvm(), kvm_get_kvm_safe(),
kvm_put_kvm() and of several VFIO exports, since vfio_main.c includes
<linux/kvm_host.h> and struct vfio_device holds a struct kvm pointer.

On arm64, KVM is built into vmlinux, and the only exported symbols
involving struct kvm are the refcounting helpers above. VFIO only passes
the struct kvm pointer back to those helpers and never accesses any of
its fields. struct kvm_smccc_features is only used internally by KVM,
and struct kvm is always allocated by the core kernel, so the size
change is not visible to modules. Thus, simply hide the change from kABI
checks.

Signed-off-by: Carlos López <clopez@suse.de>
Reviewed-by: Jan Kara <jack@suse.cz>
---
 arch/arm64/include/asm/kvm_host.h |    2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

--- a/arch/arm64/include/asm/kvm_host.h
+++ b/arch/arm64/include/asm/kvm_host.h
@@ -238,7 +238,9 @@ struct kvm_smccc_features {
 	unsigned long std_bmap;
 	unsigned long std_hyp_bmap;
 	unsigned long vendor_hyp_bmap; /* Function numbers 0-63 */
+#ifndef __GENKSYMS__
 	unsigned long vendor_hyp_bmap_2; /* Function numbers 64-127 */
+#endif
 };
 
 typedef unsigned int pkvm_handle_t;
